        "original_id": "7dd3f9cd-a993-59b1-bbec-bd338cffd62c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aleksei Gan, Nicholas II\n- Places: Russian Empire, Russia\n- Events: Russian Revolution, February Revolution of 1917\n- Roles: anarchist, avant-garde artist, art theorist, graphic designer, emperor\n- Concepts: provisional government, abdication\n\nFacts:\n- Aleksei Gan was born in either 1887 or 1893 and died in 1942.\n- Aleksei Gan was a Russian anarchist, avant-garde artist, art theorist, and graphic designer.\n- In February 1917 under the Julian calendar, which was March 1917 in the Gregorian calendar, Emperor Nicholas II abdicated during the first revolution.\n- The abdication of Nicholas II caused the collapse of the Russian Empire and the old regime was replaced by a provisional government.",
